WEBVTT

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.440
Guten Morgen!

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.480
So! You've been at True Cross Academy
for a month now.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.910
Have you gotten used to it?

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.040
Sure have!

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.500
The building's beautiful, and so are all the girls!

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.180
I'm having a lot of fun here.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.940
Good to hear.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.210
On another note, Shima.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:56.920
What would you say is a spy's most valuable asset?

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.700
That would be his skill in decieving his enemies.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:07.730
I'll be generous and give you 60 points for that.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.400
What's truly important is the information a spy obtains.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.900
Spies only lie in order to get their hands on information.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:24.660
To that end, you must also be prepared to betray your family, friends, and even yourself.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.420
In other words, a spy's heart must never waver in the pursuit of his goal.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.130
Right...

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:37.380
And on that note, I'd like to give you three special missions designed to train you.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.200
If you complete all three,
you will be duly rewarded.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.300
This will be your prize.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.340
I-Is that...

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.270
No way...

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.110
I must be seeing things, right!?

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.570
Indeed, you are gazing at that most sacred of texts,

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:04.530
the super rare compilation of the
Ecstasy Emperor's unpublished drawings!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.140
The legendary magazine that completely sold out in a single day!?

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.500
Yes.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.630
I should mention that this copy is uncensored.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.220
Uncensored...

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.060
Are you sure about this?

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.310
I mean, you're the principal.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.600
Should you even have something like this?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.230
Oh, but I'm also a demon.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.060
I'll follow you until the day I die!

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:38.420
I take it you'll accept the missions, then?

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.530
Of course!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.990
Shima!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.320
Over here.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.940
Today we're on a purification mission.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.320
Purification?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.050
What is that? It looks like the setting of a horror movie!

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.680
It used to belong to a snack company,

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:11.500
but the owner's family fought so harshly over who would inherit it

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.440
that several deaths ensued.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.140
The company later went bankrupt.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:23.700
The factories were closed, but there are lingering rumors of ghosts showing up at night.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:30.680
So you're saying that the ghosts of the people who died in those fights are here?

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.540
No.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.330
We didn't find any ghosts when we investigated the building.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.380
What we did find was an infestation of Coal Tar.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.540
Someone must have mistaken them for ghosts.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.260
Oh, is that all?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.680
Thanks to those rumors, the building won't sell.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:52.440
But just recently, the CEO of an
entertainment business became interested,

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.560
so we've been assigned to purify the building.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:02.160
Whoa, I feel like I'm in
Ghostbusters with this thing!

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.320
But Mr. Okumura, aren't Coal Tars like the weakest demons ever?

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:11.260
All they do is float around,
and most people can't even see them.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:16.100
They're completely harmless unless a bunch of them fuse together!

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.380
That's true, but the area has too many of them.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.080
Some of them may already have fused into Koks,
so I will be the one taking care of them.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.760
Wait, then what do I...

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.760
You'll be fending off the Chuchi.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.360
Uh, can you repeat that?

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.360
Chuchi.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:38.690
You mean <i>those</i> Chuchi!?

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.120
There won't be very many of them,
but they can possess cockroaches too,

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.940
so be sure to take care of those as well.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.370
I just came down with a stomachache,
so I'll pass on this one.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.960
Sorry, but I can't allow that.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.200
Why? You can do this by yourself!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.250
I'm begging you, let me go!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.860
Sir Pheles is the one who wanted you to deal with the Chuchi.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.900
He also told me to stop you from running out on the job.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.560
He said if I got sympathetic and let you leave,

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.810
he'd give me a 90% paycut.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.980
90%? How is that legal?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:22.190
Besides, what's more important,
money or your precious student!?

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:28.420
I'm sorry, but I would have a really hard time thinking of you as "precious."

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.240
And I do have bills to pay.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.280
Mr. Okumura, you demon!

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.460
I'll curse you until the day I die!

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.560
And I'll tell all your doting female fans

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:46.720
a bunch of lies about how you're super evil and have a bunch of depraved fetishes!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:53.600
No! Stop! I didn't mean it!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.220
Help!

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.650
How was it?

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:09.570
Well, I did at least learn never to piss off Mr. Okumura.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.530
That guy is a

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.640
sadist,

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.640
Get in there.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.920
demon,

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.450
and lunatic all in one!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.900
My my.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:22.790
Well, that's good enough to pass your first mission.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.240
Really?

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.250
Yes.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.720
On to the next mission.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.100
Spies must be able to adapt to any surroundings,

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:33.220
blending in as naturally as the air itself.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.260
You will eventually be assigned a very important task.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:43.350
I can assure you that this skill will prove invaluable when the time comes.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.220
Adapt how?

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:47.610
Allow me to show you.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.540
After you.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:56.200
Where does that key go?

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:59.200
Why don't you see for yourself?

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:14.390
Isn't this the dorm where the Okumura brothers live?

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.740
Ding ding ding!

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.960
This is the key to the old boys' dormitory.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.480
Why are we here, though?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.980
You will enter the dining hall,

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:28.140
eat Mr. Okumura's dinner
as casually as if it were your own,

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.900
and then stroll right back out like nothing ever happened.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.360
That will conclude your second mission.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.120
No way!

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:41.040
There's no way I can do that!

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.580
Don't worry.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.920
I gave Mr. Okumura some absurdly difficult tasks earlier,

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.840
so he'll be out for a good long while.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.970
Absurdly difficult? That makes this even worse!

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:58.200
Imagine coming home after a day like that and finding someone else eating your dinner!

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.350
Not even a saint would tolerate that!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.400
You'll be fine.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.080
Mr. Okumura is very kindhearted.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.270
I'm sure he'll simply laugh it off.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:12.400
No, no! Don't say that like you know his true nature!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:17.360
Why should I have to act like a Nurarihyon anyway?

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.760
That's not spy training,

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.540
it's just plain old theft!

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.120
Just what I'd expect from a member of Myoda!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.290
Your knowledge of Japanese folklore is impressive.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.480
Thanks, but that's not really the point.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.260
So you won't do the mission?

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.540
Not a chance.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.850
The Ecstasy Emperor's Compilation of Unpublished Drawings...

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.300
uncensored.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.360
I'll do—

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.200
Don't fall for it!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.000
I can't let myself be baited so easily!

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.420
No!

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:03.620
Stay strong!

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.040
So be it.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.680
If the carrot won't work,

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.500
I have no choice but to bring out the stick.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:22.010
Bright and early Monday morning,
I'll start selling this juicy gossip magazine.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:29.480
There are all kinds of unfounded rumors about Mr. Okumura in here,

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.720
most too nasty for me to say out loud.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:36.740
If something like this got
published right about now,

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.740
I think you know what would happen,

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.740
don't you, Shima?

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.820
I'll curse you until the day I die!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.940
And I'll tell all your doting female fans

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:52.630
a bunch of lies about how you're super evil and have a bunch of depraved fetishes!

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:56.630
<i>He's definitely going to think it was me!</i>

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.940
So, have you reconsidered?

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:05.780
Y-Yeah.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.600
I'll do it.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:11.280
I'll be happy to eat his dinner.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.810
That's what I expected.

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.180
Good evening!

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:18.960
How are you, Okumura?

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.570
Oh, Shima. What's the occasion?

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.160
Is it just you?

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.450
Where are Suguro and Konekomaru?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.380
Koneko went to some kind of club meeting,

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:30.120
and Bon is off training.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.260
Oh, I see.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:35.710
Oh man, that smells delicious!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.000
Right?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.240
I got some really good fish for half off!

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:46.180
But since there wasn't that much of it,
I added avocado as a vegetable filler.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:50.780
Hang on, Okumura, you know avocados are fruits, right?

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.740
What kind of vegetable has a pit?

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:55.980
Oh whoops! I always make that mistake!

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.640
<i>This is truly the worst-case scenario!</i>

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:04.300
<i>If he had to add filler just to make it a full meal, there can't be any extra.</i>

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:09.790
<i>If I go through with this,
Mr. Okumura won't have anything to eat tonight!</i>

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:15.280
I hate to admit it, but I overslept this morning and didn't get to make Yukio a lunch.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:19.500
And he's been so busy lately he hasn't even had time to buy food.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.050
He'll probably be starving by the time he gets back.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:26.300
He always gets grumpy when he's hungry.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:30.180
<i>Why would you tell me that now?
That's the last thing I want to hear!</i>

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:37.320
<i>But I don't think the principal was bluffing about what he'll do if I back down.</i>

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.180
<i>And then I'll be...</i>

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.260
I have no choice!

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.300
What?

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.120
Sorry. Never mind.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.950
<i>Okay, I should be able to take
advantage of how naive he is.</i>

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.860
Really though, this looks so good!

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.780
Even the colors look tasty.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:13:00.520
Are you going to become the world's best chef on top of being Paladin?

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:02.800
I don't know about that!

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:06.820
Hey Shima, what are you doing?

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.660
That's for Yukio.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.140
Oh man, it looks so good my fingers moved on their own!

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.940
Well, don't eat it.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:16.960
If you're that hungry,
I'll make you some instant ramen.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.730
Okay, I got it.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:22.360
<i>No, I can't back down now.</i>

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.190
<i>I can't!</i>

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:27.120
You sure are amazing, Okumura.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:30.600
If everyone knew how well you can cook,
I'm sure the girls would be all over you!

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:31.360
You think?

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.410
Yeah, for sure!

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:37.370
Oh, but Yukio tricked me by saying that once.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:42.590
At least I learned that hard work doesn't make you popular.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.800
Seriously, don't eat that.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.060
He's scary when he's angry.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:48.800
I know, I know!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:54.270
But Okumura, you've gotten better at cooking since then, right?

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:56.940
Well, yeah, obviously.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.880
And now that I think about it,
you're pretty easy on the eyes too.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:02.380
I wonder if you'll get a fan club sometime soon?

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.650
A fan club?

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:06.840
Wow, that would really be something!

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.620
I could finally get my turn in the spotlight!

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:15.020
The girls... the adoration... the free food!

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.500
Oh, man! That would be so great!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.820
<i>Come on, just a little more!</i>

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:21.960
<i>I need to get out of here before Mr. Okumura gets back!</i>

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:26.620
A fan club for me, though...
That could never happen!

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:30.090
Don't say that, Okumura!
Have some self-confidence!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.360
You're right!

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:33.800
Fan clubs do events, right?

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.890
And events have music, sometimes even dancing!

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:40.850
Oh, Shima, we have spoons if you want.
And I'll make you some tea.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.980
Oh, don't bother. I already finished it.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.320
Finished what?

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.400
Like I said, I'm done eating—

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:57.520
Why are you sitting in my seat and eating my dinner?

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:01.020
Surely you have a reasonable explanation for me.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:05.500
It's a long story.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.220
Let me hear it.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:12.090
I'm afraid I can't tell you.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:20.980
But won't you forgive your precious student for his innocent prank?

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.220
What?

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:31.820
Great work yesterday.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:34.910
So, how did it go?

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:41.640
He made me sit with a Bariyon
on top of my legs for two hours.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:45.340
And when that was over,
he yelled at me for another hour.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.940
How interesting.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:52.050
I guess even Mr. Okumura will hold a grudge when his food is threatened.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:56.160
So, how did you like the rice bowl?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.020
It was so good it brought me to tears.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.500
Very well.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:05.610
You had it rough, so I'll give you a passing grade.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:10.120
So, can I have the Ecstasy Emperor's Uncensored Compilation of Unpublished Drawings?

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:13.570
It's yours after you complete one final mission.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:14.540
Thank you, God!

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:15.320
I'm a demon.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.500
I'll follow you until the day I die!

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.500
That again?

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.840
Well, on to the last mission.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:27.540
To test your skills in disguise and stealth,
I'll have you infiltrate the girls' dormitory.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:32.380
If you can enter the building without having your identity found out,

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.100
I'll consider the mission complete,

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:36.500
and the magazine will be yours.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.100
Understood!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.120
Finally!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.690
I'm finally getting a real spy mission!

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:51.240
This is the free world I've been waiting for!

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:57.120
Not to mention I have the principal's permission to enter the girls' dormitory!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.080
This is too good to be true!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.400
I'm not going to fool anyone like this.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:08.660
No, wait.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.500
Doubting myself will only make it more obvious!

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.980
If I just act natural, it can still work.

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:15.580
No, I'll make it work!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:18.010
As a true man!

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.980
Sorry I called you two on your day off.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:26.120
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:31.190
You must be pretty serious to spend your day off studying calligraphy.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.180
It's nothing.

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:34.720
I got ahold of an interesting text recently,

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:37.660
but it was written in a very loose calligraphy.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:42.120
Ah, yeah, I can see why it would be hard to read if you're not used to it.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:45.680
Sir Pheles informed me that you two should be well versed in it,

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:49.060
since you're both from the temple.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:52.360
You came to the right people!
We have a book about it.

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:54.460
It should be in Shima's room.

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:56.930
Huh?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.060
Huh?

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:11.190
Shima... I didn't know you were into that.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.260
Wait, Koneko, this isn't what it looks like!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:14.100
You...

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.700
You too, Bon? Let me explain!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.320
Calm down.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:21.160
Let him explain himself.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.760
Did you have some reason to be wearing that outfit?

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:29.860
Mr. Okumura?

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:35.300
Were you planning to do something unsavory?

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.260
No! I just needed to get into the girls' dorm—

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:46.180
Well, I'm glad you confessed.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.400
Crossdressing with the intent to sneak into the girls' dormitory

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.780
is undoubtedly a crime.

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:54.900
Shima, you're despicable.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.040
You're...

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:57.620
not wrong.

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:59.780
But this isn't what you think it is! Believe me!

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:04.300
Call the police. He needs to be taken into custody.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.320
All right.

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.790
This is for his own good, right?

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.300
What are you two talking about?

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.290
You're joking, right?

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:15.550
I'm so sorry, Shima!

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.780
Don't actually call them!

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:20.040
There's no need to overreact!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.300
I'm really sorry!

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:25.760
So please hang up, Koneko!

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:32.230
B-Bon?

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:35.480
Stand up, Shima.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.650
I'll knock some sense back into you.

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.860
Don't! You'll kill me!

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.410
I'll die before I learn my lesson!

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.360
Don't worry,

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.870
once I'm done with you, I'll follow right after.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:53.640
That makes it even more worrying!
Could you please lighten up?

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:56.320
There's more to this that you're not seeing!

00:19:56.320 --> 00:20:00.880
Do you honestly think I would do something like this?

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:02.760
Yes.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.470
You monsters! I can't believe this!

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.320
Any more last words?

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:17.730
Wh—

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:20.740
What!?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:26.450
The Ecstasy Emperor's Uncensored
Compilation of Unpublished Drawings?

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:30.580
Shima, you are seriously the worst person I've ever met.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:33.900
No, wait! This is just...

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:42.420
Reading these indecent magazines is what scrambled your brains like this.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.220
You should be ashamed of yourself!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:56.020
You look happy, Brother.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.320
Do I?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.230
Yes.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:03.560
It must be because I recently
discovered a diamond in the rough.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:05.320
You mean that Renzou Shima guy?

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.530
I thought he failed all the missions you gave him?

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:14.520
There was no real meaning in the tasks I gave him.

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:19.290
I just wanted to find out if he was suitable to be my personal spy.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:23.120
As it turns out, he's perfect for it.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:26.800
He just looks like your average idiot to me.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.760
You're naive, little brother.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:35.480
He is faithful only to his own greedy desires,

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:39.140
making him a weak and shallow human,

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:41.960
yet he doesn't fear me one bit.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:48.870
He doesn't care to suck up to authority,
so he won't be easily brainwashed.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:53.330
He is truly an interesting and useful asset.

00:21:54.280 --> 00:22:01.080
I'm not looking for a soldier who will sacrifice himself to plant false information once,

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.300
but rather a spy who can report back to me many times.

00:22:05.080 --> 00:22:07.040
Do you understand, Amaimon?

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:13.500
Not really, but whatever floats your boat.

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:23.700
I'll be sure to raise you carefully.
